# `sibling` holds only the public sibling plugins' names (respeak, decisions, session, agents), so these
# entries allow nothing private. Design records, packets and ledgers name the siblings; the packets entry
# stays a glob because the relay copies each row's packet in, and a gate must not go red on a public name.
design/*.md: sibling
design/packets/*.md: sibling
design/readme/source.md: sibling
README.md: sibling
Makefile: sibling
DECISION[S].md: sibling
DESIGN.md: sibling
NICE_TO_HAVE.md: sibling
OPEN-QUESTIONS.md: sibling
decision[s]/*: sibling
# The effects, the prompt's block reader and the night's plan name the session plugin or the ledger file.
internal/effects/*.go: sibling
internal/prompt/block.go: sibling
internal/night/plan.go: sibling
# The plugin's commands and agents name an optional sibling plugin they detect.
plugin/commands/*.md: sibling
plugin/agents/*.md: sibling
# The respeak config names the plugin in its path, and this file names that path.
.claude/respeak/config.yaml: sibling
.hygiene-allow: sibling

# agentik-r1 §6.1, packet agentik-r1-relay ruling 10: the record copies of old packets keep the names they had.
internal/packet/testdata/a*.md: renamed

# The relay reads each old name while only it exists, new else old (agentik-r1 §6.3 c2-c4, c6): the state root's,
# the config layers' and the section's old spellings live in these two files, beside their new ones.
internal/effects/config.go: renamed
internal/hooks/hooks.go: renamed

